      "side": 1,
      "message": "The host map is built from `filter_hosts(retired\u003dFalse, broken\u003dFalse)` (line 471), but `hosts_range` returns schedules for every host, and retiring or breaking a host does not delete its schedules. A host missing from the active list lands here as `_model_for_host(None)` -\u003e `unknown` and still counts in `host_count` (line 175). Reproduced with one schedule for a host absent from the list: `host_count\u003d1, model_counts\u003d{\u0027unknown\u0027: 1}`. Since the window includes the previous month, recently retired hosts are the common case. Look the model up in the unfiltered host list, or skip hosts that are not active.",
      "revId": "9e2384c80df38ad89ea05dcf1b6fe50a8aefb6ab",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
